Workday was rolled out between 2015 and 2017 with the following key objectives:
– integrating our processes and systems in a two-tier architecture (global/local), such that the global level becomes the
master application for most data but local legal requirements could also be addressed;
– simplifying and standardizing processes across Business Units and support functions;
– centralizing data management on a single, unified platform, to significantly improve the quality of HR data and reporting;
– introducing self-service to enhance the user experience for employees and managers and help them engage better with
HR issues;
– improving talent management and staff mobility;
– streamlining IT mapping;

Sanofi carried out the following bond issues during the period:
• March 2025: a bond issue of €1.5 billion in two tranches;
• June 2025: a bond issue of €1.5 billion in two tranches;
• November 2025: a bond issue of $3.0 billion in five tranches;

Three bond issues were redeemed in 2025:
• the €1 billion fixed-rate bond issue from April 2020, which was redeemed at maturity on April 1, 2025;
• the €850 million fixed-rate bond issue from April 2022, which was redeemed at maturity on April 6, 2025; and
• the €750 million fixed-rate bond issue from September 2015, which was redeemed at maturity on September 22, 2025;
